# NOTE: git does NOT support inline (end-of-line) comments in .gitignore.
# Every comment lives on its own line. Provenance for the vendored repos below
# is in README.md -> "Vendored dependencies".

# ── Secrets — never commit (a vast private key was found in the repo root once) ──
vast_ssh_key
vast_ssh_key.pub
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.env
.env.*

# ── Infra state — per-machine, regenerated each rental ──
.instance_id

# ── Installed dev skills / local Claude Code config (pinned by skills-lock.json) ──
.agents/
.claude/

# ── Vendored third-party GitHub repos (NOT ours to redistribute) ──
# github.com/anthropics/jacobian-lens @ 581d398
jacobian-lens/
# twoxtwo_repo, hawthorne, nguyen (vendored datasets)
recon/data/
recon/tok/
# vendored HF tokenizer caches

# ── Third-party / harmful-content benchmark data — never redistribute (BUILD §9) ──
# EvalAwareBench-derived prompt corpora (large; contain harmful-content eval items)

# Pile-component corpus plaintext: licensed (CC-BY-SA / Common Crawl / GitHub).
# Ship the builder + manifest, never the text. manifest.json IS committed and records
# per-file SHA-256, window count and the disjoint seed-block ranges, so the exact pool
# is reconstructible with:  python build_corpora.py
corpora/*.jsonl

# ── Model artifacts — large; SHA-256 in ARTIFACTS.md, backed up off-box ──
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.bin

# ── Large / regenerable data ──
*.zip

# ── Python caches, build artifacts, virtualenvs ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
**/.venv*/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── OS / editor junk ──
.DS_Store
*.swp

# vendored jlens copy inside jspace vetting bundle

# transient GPU-box result pull staging (rsync)

# E1 session: third-party operator-hunt clones (never committed)
workspace/
.instance_id.destroyed-*

# freshly cloned public J-lens implementations (re-fetch, never modify in place)
thirdparty/

# LaTeX build products. `paper/` and `specs/` hold the SOURCE, which IS tracked; these are
# everything pdflatex leaves behind. There was a bare `paper/` rule here until 2026-08-15,
# from the E1 arc, which would now ignore the NeurIPS submission source itself.
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.pdf

# lab / repro runtime state (machine-specific, never shared)
.fleet
.pull_receipt_*.json

# E35 containment worker bitmaps — 12 MB derived binary, regenerable in ~15 min from
# EleutherAI/pile-deduped-pythia-preshuffled shard 0. SHA-256 recorded in ARTIFACTS.md.
results/found_shard0.tgz

# ── results/ CUT-OVER, staged 2026-08-15, NOT YET FIRED ──
# The results JSON is the record of record and currently lives in git (418 files, ~8 MB).
# It is also being mirrored to Hugging Face. Uncomment this block ONLY after
#   bash repro/04_fetch_results.sh --check
# reports 0 missing, then `git rm -r --cached results`. Order matters: the window in which
# results exist in neither place is the failure this staging exists to prevent.
# results/*.json
# results/*/*.json
# results/*/*.npz
repro/lib/__pycache__/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# results/ is mirrored to the private HF repo ${HF_REPO}
# and untracked from git as of 2026-08-22. The last commit carrying them is
# e26993c ("saving commit before repo cleanup"), so the history is intact.
# Sync with:  .venv/bin/python tools/hf_sync_results.py --push
# Fetch with: repro/04_fetch_results.sh
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/

# The double-blind gate reads its literal identity strings from here. Untracked ON PURPOSE:
# shipping the pattern list would republish the strings the gate exists to remove.
tools/deanon_patterns.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PAPER IS NOT PUBLISHED WITH THE CODE.
#
# The submission is double-blind and the artifact repository is supplementary material. The .tex
# carries the manuscript argument, the build carries an [anonymised repository url] placeholder, and
# paper/ARGUMENT.md and paper/PAPER_HANDOFF.md are working documents in the first person. None of
# that belongs in the reviewer-visible artifact, and keeping it out is cheaper than scrubbing it.
#
# The paper still builds locally: paper/ is untracked, not deleted. `cd paper && ./build_audit.sh`
# is unaffected. Only the PUBLISHED tree loses it.
paper/

# Release plan and the review behind it: local working documents, not part of the
# published artifact. They name a contributor and describe the anonymisation procedure.
instructions/
docs/reviews/REPO_REVIEW_2026-08-29.md
repro/t1_sweep/_run/

# Hugging Face release metadata. These ship at the ROOT of the artifact mirror
# (LICENSE / ATTRIBUTION.md / README.md), not in the code repository, which has its own.
release_meta/

# ── maintainer-only anonymisation tooling: NEVER publish ──
# tools/build_anon_staging.py embeds the deanonymisation patterns (the identity strings and
# home path) exactly as tools/deanon_patterns.json does. Publishing the scrubber publishes the
# thing it scrubs for. tools/hf_release_push.py is retired push tooling that names the old mirror.
tools/build_anon_staging.py
tools/hf_release_push.py

# Root working note from a handoff session. NOT docs/context/CONTEXT.md (which is the tracked,
# reviewer-facing one). This copy carries the laptop hostname in prose and must never ship.
/CONTEXT.md


docs/reproducibility/REVIEWER.md
docs/validity/AUDIT_READINESS.md

